              {
                "choice_label": "D",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=6-4\\cos(6t)+\\sin(6t)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=6-4\\cos(3t)-\\sin(3t)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "B"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$x(t)=6-4\\cos(3t)+\\sin(3t)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Use the reconstruction rule: write the DC term once as $a_0/2$, then place $a_1$ on $\\cos(\\omega_0 t)$ and $b_1$ on $\\sin(\\omega_0 t)$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "x(t)=\\frac{12}{2}+(-4)\\cos(3t)+1\\sin(3t)=6-4\\cos(3t)+\\sin(3t)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "So the reconstructed signal is $x(t)=6-4\\cos(3t)+\\sin(3t)$. The main check is that $a_0$ is halved and the first-harmonic coefficients stay attached to the correct trigonometric terms.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "question_index": 2,
            "question_type": "multiple-choice",
            "answer_cardinality": "single",
            "prompt_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Reconstruct $x(t)$ when $a_0=14$, $a_1=3$, $b_1=-2$, and $\\omega_0=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [
              {
                "choice_label": "A",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=7+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)+2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "B",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=14+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)-2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "C",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=7-2\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)+3\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "D",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=7+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)-2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": true
              },
              {
                "choice_label": "E",
                "choice_blocks": [
                  {
                    "block_type": "paragraph",
                    "text": "$x(t)=7+3\\cos(\\pi t)-2\\sin(\\pi t)$",
                    "latex": "",
                    "image_slot_id": ""
                  }
                ],
                "is_correct": false
              }
            ],
            "correct_choice_labels": [
              "D"
            ],
            "correct_answer": "$x(t)=7+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)-2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Again, use $x(t)=a_0/2+a_1\\cos(\\omega_0 t)+b_1\\sin(\\omega_0 t)$. The DC term becomes $14/2=7$, and the first harmonic uses $\\omega_0 t=\\frac{\\pi t}{2}$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "x(t)=\\frac{14}{2}+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)+(-2)\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)=7+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)-2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "So the reconstructed signal is $x(t)=7+3\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)-2\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{2}\\right)$. The main checks are the half-factor on $a_0$ and keeping the first harmonic at $\\omega_0 t$, not $2\\omega_0 t$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
